title: Palindrome
golf: 46

Write `palindrome(word)` that returns `True` if the word reads the same backwards.
Ignore capitals: `palindrome("Racecar")` gives `True`.
=== starter
def palindrome(word):
    ...
=== broken
def palindrome(word):
    word = word.lower()
    return word == word.reverse()
=== test
from harness import eq


def test_palindrome(sol):
    eq(sol.palindrome("Racecar"), True, 'palindrome("Racecar")')
    eq(sol.palindrome("level"), True, 'palindrome("level")')
    eq(sol.palindrome("python"), False, 'palindrome("python")')
